          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4b2095aad44f4f946d73ae2a7142566f236a89ff27b23c6065cc0cedd671aa0e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2d8b7076953f4976b6db33d29370588f",
      "statement": "The CLI's setup runner (runSetup) executes steps sequentially, halting on failure. Each step has a check (is it already done?) and an apply (make it so). After applying, it re-checks with specific backoff delays of [0, 300, 700, 2000, 4000, 8000] ms (totaling 15 seconds) to handle admin-node/service-node propagation lag. Dry runs execute all checks without applying. The force option skips checks but still verifies the result via re-check.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/cli/src/setup.ts#L108-L246",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:06581a6826f7a04f4cf50d4aeac5365f7c77a2f509cc9ec696fe4c5178320589:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/cli/src/setup.ts#L155-L189",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:68c2c0559fce01323f31ca3e1f68f9455169209a3709573d4ca32f8bb558f517:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f613d76a3f7247388da0b9973bc6768d",
      "statement": "The CLI stores personal access tokens in ~/.config/ulabase/session.json (or XDG_CONFIG_HOME) with 0600 permissions. The ULABASE_TOKEN environment variable always takes precedence over the stored session, ensuring CI pipelines never silently use a stale credential.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/cli/src/cli.ts",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:197e73467a15e723338ed6b08680cd532d797637307203bfd9d1bcbfff35bb3b"
