          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bd8bc617330284d658834edd53ee90af706dad96750de693a4775eced44e4e59:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_857c3b6e9ab84cffab62e7ea5afee7ec",
      "statement": "Unlike acceptConsents, switchTeam, and updateProfile, a subscription change does not trigger a token renewal. The @subscription ACL variable is resolved server-side from the database on every request, cached only for the life of that request, so an upgrade is effective immediately with no re-login.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/kit/src/payments.ts#L5-L23",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:962eca90cb942c43ad576a8c123f01f6dbc178435aa4438d0a410873d5aeed90:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0d80b2812eb749fb96a81a7422de80cb",
      "statement": "The cart (cart.ts) is a pure client-side data structure — addToCart, setCartQuantity, removeFromCart, and cartTotals are pure functions that return new arrays and never talk to a server. toOrderItems strips display fields and passes only productId, quantity, and metadata to createOrder. Prices in the cart are display-only; the service reads unit_amount from its own catalog.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/kit/src/cart.ts#L1-L14",
